- The normalization step (padding to a square size) is ambiguous; the examples show shapes are not simply padded but may be resized or transformed.
- The rule assumes a one-to-one mapping from distinct shapes to columns, but examples show multiple tiles of the same shape in the same output.

The rule lacks generality and does not capture the true underlying transformation, which likely involves more complex object-based rearrangements, possibly involving recursion or hierarchical composition.

