The output is formed by taking the binary mask of the smallest connected object (by cell count) among the non‑background colors, within its bounding box. The two most frequent colors (by total area) among the large solid blocks are chosen. The mask is repeated horizontally to match the width of the larger block (or a multiple thereof), with 1’s mapped to the first color and 0’s to the second. The output height equals the mask height.

