### Revised Rule

Find the largest solid rectangle of color 8 that touches any edge of the input grid. If multiple exist with the same area, choose the one that appears first in row-major order. Let its dimensions be H (height) and W (width). The output is the central H×W subgrid of the input (centered both vertically and horizontally), rotated 180 degrees (i.e., reversed in both row and column order).

