Revised Rule:
The transformation detects all **connected components (objects) of color 4** that contain at least one **“plus‑seed”** — a cell of color 4 whose four orthogonal neighbors are all also color 4 (forming a 5‑cell plus).  
When such a plus‑seed exists in a component, the **entire connected component of 4s** is recolored to color 8.  
If a component of 4s contains no plus‑seed, it is left unchanged.

In other words:  
1. Identify all 4‑connected regions of cells with value 4.  
2. For each region, check whether any cell in that region has its up, down, left, right neighbors all equal to 4 (all inside the region).  
3. If yes, change every cell in that region to 8.  
4. All other cells (including other colors) remain unchanged.

