### Proposed Rule
Identify all rectangular frames: contiguous regions of a single non-background color that form a hollow rectangle (border cells of that color, interior cells are background or other colors). The frame must have thickness 1 (only border cells). In output, keep only these frames, removing all other non-background cells. Additionally, for each frame, in the middle row of its interior (the row exactly between top and bottom borders), set the cell to the frame's color at every interior column where the column offset from the left border is even (i.e., (col - left_col) % 2 == 0). The interior columns are those strictly between left and right borders.

