Revision Raw Output:
### Revised Rule

The transformation identifies each contiguous region (object) of non-zero color (connected via 4-neighbors) in the input. For each object, we compute its bounding box (min row, max row, min col, max col). Then we draw the outline of that bounding box with the object's color, and also fill the interior of the bounding box with the same color, but only if the object originally consisted of more than one cell. If the object is a single isolated cell, we instead draw a cross shape (plus sign) centered at that cell: the horizontal and vertical arms extending to the edges of a 3×3 area (i.e., the cell itself and its four orthogonal neighbors) are set to that color.

Additionally, if two or more objects of the same color have overlapping bounding boxes (or are adjacent such that their bounding boxes touch or overlap), they are merged into a single combined bounding box, and the outline and fill are applied to the union.

Finally, after processing all objects, any cell that receives multiple colors (due to overlapping outlines/fills) is resolved by taking the maximum color value among the contenders.

