### Proposed Rule
For each row, identify the contiguous horizontal segment of non‑zero colors that ends immediately left of the vertical line (i.e., the cell at (row, line_col‑1) is non‑zero). Let L be the length of the run of the rightmost color within that segment (at least 1). Starting at the first cell to the right of the line, place that rightmost color every L cells (i.e., at columns line_col+1, line_col+1+L, line_col+1+2L, ...) until the grid boundary. If L=1, fill all cells to the right with that color.

