5. The overall output grid is the concatenation of all such processed blocks, arranged in the same relative order as they appear in the input (left-to-right, top-to-bottom), but with each block resized to its inner shape's bounding box.

6. Blocks that do not contain an inner shape (i.e., are solid) are omitted from the output.

In the training examples, the input grid has a background color (8 in example 1, 2 in example 2) that separates the blocks. Each block is processed independently.

