### Proposed Rule  
For each color that appears in the top row (excluding the vertical separator column and zeros), if there is a connected shape of that color in the left region (cols left of separator), remove that shape. Then, for each occurrence of that color in the top row, place a 3×3 plus sign (cross) of that color in the right region, centered at the column of that occurrence and at a row equal to the centroid row of the original shape (or if multiple original shapes, the first one). If the plus sign would extend outside the right region bounds, adjust minimally to fit.

