Identify the background color as the color of the top‑left cell. Find all columns where every cell is the same color and that color is not the background. If there are at least two such columns, extract the columns strictly between the first two (excluding those delimiter columns). If there is exactly one such column, extract all columns before it (excluding that column). If there are no such columns, output the entire input grid unchanged.

