### Proposed Rule
Identify a rectangular region (the "zero band") where all cells are color 0 except one column (the "marker column") which contains some colored cells. The output grid has the same height and width as this region, initially filled with 0. For each colored cell in the marker column, let its color be c and let n be the number of distinct connected components (objects) of color c in the input outside the zero band. In the output row corresponding to that cell's row within the band, place color c in every other column starting from the leftmost column, exactly n times.

