2. **Recolor the interior of this border** (i.e., all cells inside the closed border, including the border cells themselves) to a new color. The new color is determined by the most frequent color among the cells that are immediately outside the border (i.e., cells adjacent to the border but not part of the dominant object). If there are multiple such colors with the same frequency, choose the smallest color value.

Additionally, any other objects (contiguous regions) that are completely surrounded by the dominant object (i.e., holes inside it) are left unchanged.

