### Revised Rule
For each solid rectangular block of height H and width W (H,W>1), determine its "source color" as the color of the nearest single‑cell object (1×1 connected component) that lies in the same column as the block’s leftmost column and in a row above the block. If no such single cell exists, use the color of the nearest single‑cell object in the same column below the block. Then replicate the block downward with a vertical gap of H‑1 rows, painting each copy with that source color, as many times as fits within the grid.

