### Revised Rule

The transformation identifies each distinct colored object (connected component via 4-connectivity) in the input grid, ignoring the background color (which is the most frequent color in the grid). For each object, compute its **vertical extent**: the number of distinct rows that contain at least one cell of that object. Then, in the output, list each object in order of first appearance (row-major order) as a vertical block of its color, with the block height equal to its vertical extent. The output is a single column containing these stacked blocks.

