For each 5x5 block in the 19x19 grid (blocks are at rows 1-5, 7-11, 13-17 and columns similarly), identify the two colors present. Let color A be the color that appears in the four corners of the input block (if not uniform, take the color that appears in the majority of corners; if tie, take the color in the top-left corner). Let color B be the other color. In the output block, set all cells to color B, and set the four corner cells to color A.

